<refentry id="systemd-firstboot-generator" conditional='ENABLE_FIRSTBOOT'
    xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

  <refentryinfo>
    <title>systemd-firstboot-generator</title>
    <productname>systemd</productname>
  </refentryinfo>

  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>systemd-firstboot-generator</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>8</manvolnum>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>systemd-firstboot-generator</refname>
    <refpurpose>Detach a headless <filename>systemd-firstboot.service</filename> from the console</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>

  <refsynopsisdiv>
    <para><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/system-generators/systemd-firstboot-generator</filename></para>
  </refsynopsisdiv>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para>By default,
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-firstboot.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
    connects to <filename>/dev/console</filename> in order to prompt the user. It fails to start if the
    system has no console.</para>

    <para>If prompting is disabled via the <varname>systemd.firstboot=</varname> kernel command line option,
    <filename>systemd-firstboot-generator</filename> connects the service's stdin to
    <filename>/dev/null</filename> instead, and its stdout/err to the journal and to the console, if there
    is one. This way, settings passed in via
    credentials are applied on systems without a console, too.</para>

    <para><filename>systemd-firstboot-generator</filename> implements
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.generator</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Kernel Command Line</title>

    <variablelist class='kernel-commandline-options'>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>systemd.firstboot=</varname></term>

        <listitem><para>If set to a false boolean value or <literal>headless</literal>,
        <filename>systemd-firstboot.service</filename> is detached from the console. See
        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-firstboot</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
        for the meaning of this option.</para>

        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v263"/></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>See Also</title>
    <para><simplelist type="inline">
      <member><citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry></member>
      <member><citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-firstboot</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry></member>
      <member><citerefentry><refentrytitle>kernel-command-line</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry></member>
    </simplelist></para>
  </refsect1>

</refentry>
